.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:104: - **Member management** — **no** add/remove/invite tools. So automated volunteer offboarding is NOT possible (resolves the old `[VERIFY]`) → the NGO removes the volunteer manually at completion. ai4good is never a member of the NGO's Lovable workspace (seat dropped, #2 below).
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:209: - **Role model (verified against Lovable's full workspace role matrix, 2026-07-13).** From the matrix: *Create new projects in a workspace* = Editor **Yes**; *Manage Supabase* (enable/manage the DB) = Editor **Yes**; *Manage GitHub* = Editor Yes; *Publish* = Editor Yes; *Manage plans & billing* = Editor **No**; *Manage Integrations* (workspace-level connectors) = Editor **No**; *View usage* = Editor **No**. Only *Disconnect Supabase* (destructive, project-level) is admin/owner. So the volunteer is invited as **Editor** and does the **entire technical setup**; the NGO's role collapses to account/billing. (The PRD states these as capabilities — "build-only member with no billing access", "read-only monitoring account with no billing or admin access" — the verified Lovable mechanism for both is the **Editor** role; d56.) Kickoff split:
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:210:   - **NGO owner (account/billing only):** create workspace + plan + card; **set the volunteer's per-member `monthly_credit_limit`** (native Lovable spend cap, UI-only, no MCP setter); invite the volunteer as **Editor**; add a workspace-level connector only if a specific project needs one (*Manage Integrations* is admin/owner).
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:214: - **Credit-display read mechanism — server-side bot (INTENDED, conditional on the `[verify]` below; founder 2026-07-13, d50).** Preferred over the volunteer's in-session read, which is fragile and dev-machine-dependent. Design: a dedicated **ai4good bot Lovable account** is an **editor** member of each NGO workspace; a **server runs headless Claude Code** with the Lovable MCP authed once (browser) as the bot; a **skill loops `get_workspace` over the active-project `workspace_id` list**, computes OK/low/exhausted, and POSTs to an ai4good edge function → per-project cache → UI (REQ-010). Why it's buildable despite Lovable exposing no server/machine auth (OAuth-only, whitelisted clients, no API keys — verified): **Claude Code is a whitelisted OAuth client**, so headless Claude Code is a *supported* client, not a custom server (which Lovable blocks). Editor role keeps billing locked. **Invites + gate (d51):** the **NGO performs both invites** — the ai4good read-only bot (editor) *and* the volunteer (editor). Not the volunteer or an operator: the headless bot has **no way to invite anyone** (no member-management MCP verb — inviting is dashboard-only; an editor *account* has the permission, but only a human at the dashboard can exercise it, and the bot is headless). **Both memberships are a hard kickoff gate** (folds into the REQ-024 "Lovable setup pending" blocker / REQ-005.5 kickoff): the volunteer cannot start and project state cannot progress to active build until both are confirmed — so the platform is **never building blind** to Lovable credit consumption + state (the monitoring bot is provably present before credits are spent). Confirmation: the **bot self-confirms** via a successful `get_workspace`; the **volunteer's** membership is confirmed via their own session / validated paste-back (`[verify]` — no member-list API to enumerate members). The read-only editor bot **bounds** platform visibility to exactly credit-consumption + state (least-privilege). Offboarding removes both (dashboard). A Lovable **member-management API** would remove both manual invites — part of the durable ask.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:217:   - **Pure-doc MEMBERSHIP fold — DONE (d52, 2026-07-13).** Scrubbed the now-false "ai4good is never a member / nothing to remove / no member seat" language across the PRD (REQ-008, REQ-010, REQ-012, REQ-021, REQ-005.5, Story 6, s9 risk). The PRD now states: ai4good runs a **read-only monitoring account** (editor role, no billing/admin) in each NGO workspace; the **NGO invites both** the volunteer and the monitoring account at kickoff, **both validated before the volunteer starts**; **offboarding removes both**; credit status is read via the monitoring account (not the volunteer's session). What stays in these notes (NOT in the PRD): the **read MECHANISM** — headless Claude Code as the monitoring account — which is still conditional on the `[verify — make-or-break]` token-persistence proof above. If that proof fails and the bot is dropped, the membership statements revert.
.taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:218:   - `[still pending]` a roadmap item for the **durable Lovable service-account / API-key + member-management API** (formalize as an RM referenced from the pure doc to keep the RM bijection) — the headless-Claude-Code setup is the interim. Raise that ask with Lovable in parallel (their docs invite "contact support for alternative authentication").
