    1: # Routes
    2: 
    3: TanStack Start uses **file-based routing**. Every `.tsx` file in this directory
    4: is a route. Do **not** create `src/pages/`, `src/routes/_app/index.tsx`, or
    5: `app/layout.tsx` â€” those are Next.js / Remix conventions. The only root layout
    6: is `src/routes/__root.tsx`.
    7: 
    8: ## Conventions
    9: 
   10: | File | URL |
   11: | --- | --- |
   12: | `index.tsx` | `/` |
   13: | `about.tsx` | `/about` |
   14: | `users/index.tsx` | `/users` |
   15: | `users/$id.tsx` | `/users/:id` (dynamic â€” bare `$`, no curly braces) |
   16: | `posts/{-$category}.tsx` | `/posts/:category?` (optional segment) |
   17: | `files/$.tsx` | `/files/*` (splat â€” read via `_splat` param, never `*`) |
   18: | `_layout.tsx` | layout route (renders children via `<Outlet />`) |
   19: | `__root.tsx` | app shell â€” wraps every page; preserve `<Outlet />` |
   20: 
   21: `routeTree.gen.ts` is auto-generated. Don't edit it by hand.
