.taskmaster\docs\prd.md:1550: **Workspace provisioning — pool model (decision-20 amendment, 2026-07-05):** Linear's free plan includes API + webhook access, unlimited members, 2 teams, and a 250-active-issue cap — verified at docs level 2026-07-05; the first project workspace doubles as the empirical test. **Workspace creation has no public API**, so creation is moved OFF the kickoff critical path: the concierge **pre-creates a pool of ready workspaces in batch** (neutral names `a4g-pool-N`; per workspace: platform API key → Vault, webhook registered → secret in Vault, GitHub integration pre-connected to `ai4good-projects` with all-repositories scope so later-created repos are picked up automatically). **Kickoff is then API-only:** assign the next `ready` pool workspace to the project, rename it (`organizationUpdate` — `name` + `urlKey`; Linear keeps + redirects prior URL keys), set the team key to the project slug, invite the volunteer, push the decomposition. A `linear_pool_replenish` ops_task fires when the ready pool drops below the watermark (default 3) — the concierge tops up on their own schedule instead of blocking a kickoff. Pool empty at kickoff = `external_dependency` blocker + urgent replenish task (the only stall mode). **Two [VERIFY] items on the first pool batch:** (a) `organizationUpdate` rename works on the free tier via the workspace API key; (b) the pre-connected GitHub integration sees repos created after connection. **Honest note:** bulk-provisioned empty workspaces sharpen — not soften — the fair-use question; the "written blessing from Linear" probe is a stronger prerequisite under the pool model than it was per-project.
