loop\items\AI4DEV-58\artifacts\gate1-sol.stderr.log:1944:   65:  * exception would invite a caller to treat "a volunteer may not do this" the same way it treats a
loop\items\AI4DEV-58\artifacts\gate1-sol.stderr.log:6258: .taskmaster\docs\architecture-notes.md:209: - **Role model (verified against Lovable's full workspace role matrix, 2026-07-13).** From the matrix: *Create new projects in a workspace* = Editor **Yes**; *Manage Supabase* (enable/manage the DB) = Editor **Yes**; *Manage GitHub* = Editor Yes; *Publish* = Editor Yes; *Manage plans & billing* = Editor **No**; *Manage Integrations* (workspace-level connectors) = Editor **No**; *View usage* = Editor **No**. Only *Disconnect Supabase* (destructive, project-level) is admin/owner. So the volunteer is invited as **Editor** and does the **entire technical setup**; the NGO's role collapses to account/billing. (The PRD states these as capabilities — "build-only member with no billing access", "read-only monitoring account with no billing or admin access" — the verified Lovable mechanism for both is the **Editor** role; d56.) Kickoff split:
loop\items\AI4DEV-58\artifacts\gate1-sol.stderr.log:6379: .taskmaster\docs\prd-new.md:319: - **Lovable path (v1 default):** the platform does not pre-create the repo at funding. Kickoff auto-raises a Lovable-setup blocker, and the NGO (workspace + admin invite) and volunteer (GitHub install + connector + paste-back) work an 11-step checklist that the platform auto-validates, recording the repo URL — typically same-day, with aging escalation if either party stalls. No platform-admin involvement. The repo URL is a hard handoff precondition.
loop\items\AI4DEV-58\artifacts\gate1-sol.stderr.log:6389: .taskmaster\docs\prd-new.md:417: 2. Setup is mandatory at kickoff: a blocking setup item is auto-raised to the NGO. The NGO and volunteer complete it through the existing blocker + comment surfaces; the platform admin has zero per-project involvement, and the NGO needs no GitHub account. The checklist: the NGO signs up (a paid Lovable tier is required for the workspace-admin role), creates the workspace/project seeded from a one-click-copied scope summary, and invites the volunteer as workspace admin **plus the platform's ops account as a member (decision-35 — one more one-click invite; this seat powers automated offboarding at handoff/abandonment and exits at handoff)**; the volunteer accepts, connects Lovable's GitHub sync so the repo is created inside the platform's GitHub org, and pastes back the workspace/repo identifiers; the platform auto-validates (repo in the platform org, repo flipped public after validation, platform GitHub App installed, name collisions surfaced, volunteer repo permission normalized so they cannot add collaborators unnoticed), auto-resolves the item, seeds the repo template, and notifies both parties.
loop\items\AI4DEV-58\artifacts\gate1-sol.stderr.log:6394: .taskmaster\docs\prd-new.md:509: **Provisioning — pool model:** Linear workspace creation has no public API, so the concierge pre-creates a pool of ready workspaces in batch, each pre-wired for platform access, events, and GitHub integration. Kickoff then needs no manual step: assign the next ready workspace, rename it for the project, invite the volunteer, and seed the PRD bootstrap task (REQ-036 — the build tree arrives post-gate). A replenishment task fires when the ready pool drops below a watermark (default 3); an empty pool at kickoff raises an external-dependency blocker — the only stall mode. Honest note: bulk-provisioned empty workspaces sharpen — not soften — the fair-use question. The written blessing from Linear is POSTPONED to a pool scale-out gate (founder verdict, flow #20 2026-07-08): the pilot's handful of workspaces proceeds on ordinary free-tier terms, risk accepted, with the paid tier as the fallback if Linear ever objects.
loop\items\AI4DEV-58\artifacts\gate1-sol.stderr.log:6395: .taskmaster\docs\prd-new.md:515: **Write authority (real-signals enforcement):** volunteers and their agents may read, comment, and self-assign — never change status. The GitHub integration moves status on PR events. The platform creates issues (decomposition; in v1, scope-addition tasks are volunteer-created per REQ-025), invites members, reverts, and cancels. The NGO holds no Linear seat — its visibility is the Status Panel exclusively. Because OAuth scopes cannot express "assign + comment but not status," enforcement is detect-and-revert: any status change not made by the GitHub integration, and lacking a linked merged PR, is automatically reverted with an explanatory comment and a low-tone notification to the volunteer (a restricted read/assign/comment proxy is held in reserve if reverting proves noisy). Agent actions are attributed to the volunteer — human vs agent is indistinguishable and accepted; the volunteer owns their agents' actions.
loop\items\AI4DEV-58\artifacts\gate1-sol.stderr.log:6535: .taskmaster\docs\acceptance\at-req-021.md:65: - **AT-021.32 (P0)** — Given the NGO runs the account/billing setup, When it creates the workspace, funds it, sets the credit cap, and sends both invites, Then all succeed with ZERO platform-admin actions and NO NGO GitHub account or credential anywhere in the flow; and the two invitation events carry timestamps INSIDE the kickoff-setup window, before the membership gate releases the volunteer — invitation timing asserted, not assumed. [cx: added] [cx r2: kickoff-timing timestamps added — no test observed WHEN the invites happen]
